-- Two rules of one name, each with a TYPICALLY default, in sibling sections.
-- The entry `presumed` gives for a default names the rule behind the heading it
-- is declared under, so the three rows (Alpha's rate 3, Beta's rate 5, both)
-- list `Alpha.scaled`, `Beta.scaled` and both, instead of one `scaled` for all
-- three (overnight card O6, 2026-10-11). The exported rule is at the top level
-- so that it has no heading of its own.

@export default Combine
GIVEN useAlpha IS A BOOLEAN
      useBeta  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE combine IS
  (IF useAlpha THEN `Alpha`.scaled WITH base IS 10 ELSE 0)
    PLUS (IF useBeta THEN `Beta`.scaled WITH base IS 10 ELSE 0)

§ `Alpha`

GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3
      base IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled MEANS rate TIMES base

§ `Beta`

GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 5
      base IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled MEANS rate TIMES base
